Iberian margins are supported by structural fundamentals: surplus refining capacity (121% / 103% of oil demand in Spain / Portugal) provides secure, low-cost domestic supply, while c.36% cheaper industrial power lowers refining and site costs vs. core European peers. A lighter tax burden (Spain 49% / 44% of petrol / diesel pump price vs. 54% / 50% EU-27) lets operators hold margin while keeping pump prices competitive
